    <h1>Why Every Bottle<br>Has a Journey</h1>
  </section>

  <article class="essay">
    <p>We never wanted YaadWine to be another wine review page.</p>

    <p>Here's the truth: we got tired of the wine world acting like everything just... appeared. Like a grape simply belongs somewhere, the way a fact belongs in an encyclopedia. Malbec is Argentine. Chenin Blanc is from the Loire. Full stop. End of sentence. Nothing more to ask.</p>

    <p>But nothing in wine just appeared.</p>

    <p>Someone had to carry a vine across an ocean.</p>

    <p>Someone had to learn a new climate the hard way, one bad harvest at a time.</p>

    <p>Someone built the irrigation that makes the whole wine system possible, and their name isn't on the label.</p>

    <p>Someone bet everything on a grape that history had already given up on.</p>

    <p>I think about this because we all came from somewhere and something, then evolve into this.</p>

    <p>I'm Jamaican—heritage and birth—living in New York, and I got into wine here, immersed in a world that mostly doesn't look like me or think about people who look like me. And that's changing.</p>

    <p>So when we started digging into wine, we kept noticing the same pattern everywhere we looked.</p>

    <p>Grapes have migration stories.</p>

    <p>Regions have migration stories.</p>

    <p>And almost always, if you dig one layer past the tasting notes, there's a person—or a whole people—who did the actual work and never got the credit. Sometimes they chose to move. Sometimes they didn't get a choice at all. Either way, most wine writing skips straight past them to get to the part about tannins and the many likes on social media.</p>

    <p class="pull-quote">We won't skip that part.</p>

    <p>That's YaadWine.</p>

    <p>Not a wine blog.</p>

    <p>Not tasting notes with jokes attached... well, maybe you'll see some of that.</p>

    <p>This is where we tell you the whole story of a bottle—the fun parts and the parts that make you sit for a second, think, and drink on it—because we think you deserve the whole truth, not just the version that gets the most likes.</p>

    <p>Every bottle has a journey.</p>

    <p>We just happen to think you should know who also made the journey with the bottle.</p>
  </article>

  <section class="essay-close">
    <p class="closing-line">— Welcome to YaadWine.</p>
